#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:14
msgid "Diagnostics, output privacy, and model selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:16
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The logging module provides a common logger factory, delayed/idempotent "
"setup, rotating plaintext file diagnostics, stderr output, optional run-"
"event sinks, and a structured `LogExtra` restricted to flat scalar "
"values. Its secret filter scrubs messages, %-format arguments, "
"exceptions, and extra fields; it recognizes sensitive key names and "
"assignments, bearer/API tokens, base64-like document payloads, and "
"operator home-directory prefixes. It recursively handles common "
"containers and stringifies opaque objects only to check whether their "
"rendering exposes a payload or home path. Large raw byte arguments are "
"replaced. Separate handler filters suppress run-event duplication and "
"operator-document echoes on stderr, and hold third-party DEBUG records "
"below disk sinks. Record scrubbing (`src/cadrumo/core/logging.py`) "
"SecretScrubbingFilter (`src/cadrumo/core/logging.py`) Third-party DEBUG "
"filter (`src/cadrumo/core/logging.py`) Handler configuration "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/logging.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:18
msgid ""
"Startup avoids loading settings for CLI help/version, defers "
"configuration until dispatch when requested, buffers a bounded number of "
"low-severity records before setup, and falls back to stderr-only if the "
"diagnostic directory cannot be created. Logging refuses to inspect a "
"former product-state root while that typed refusal is active. These are "
"best-effort diagnostics rather than the structured command-result "
"contract. The file logs are plaintext and are not encrypted by this "
"module. One conditional gap is visible at the run-sink seam: "
"`attach_run_sink` installs the secret scrubber but not the third-party "
"DEBUG filter, despite the latter's rationale describing categorical "
"suppression at every disk sink. If a run sink accepts propagated third-"
"party DEBUG records, the categorical block does not apply there; safety "
"then depends on the scrubber recognizing what the third-party record "
"renders. This deserves a call-site/sink-level check. Configuration "
"degradation and state refusal (`src/cadrumo/core/logging.py`) Run-sink "
"attachment (`src/cadrumo/core/logging.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:20
msgid ""
"`output_rendering.py` is the separate success-output boundary: it returns"
" already-redacted text for text or JSON mode, handles safe conversions "
"for dates, paths, decimals and sets, and refuses unsupported "
"objects/formats through typed errors. Profile and bucket identifiers "
"remain redacted by default; an explicit setting opts into revealing only "
"those opaque identifiers, while tax identities, URLs, tokens, and secure-"
"object keys stay redacted. The returned model retains rendered text "
"rather than the original payload, so a later transport cannot casually "
"bypass this pass. Error envelopes and logs use other boundaries. Central "
"renderer (`src/cadrumo/core/output_rendering.py`) Identifier opt-in "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/output_rendering.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:22
msgid ""
"`model_catalogue.py` records local Ollama and hosted Anthropic candidates"
" for vision transcription, text extraction, column-role mapping, and "
"supply-nature proposals. Candidates declare runtime-specific ordering "
"costs (local memory requirement or hosted input price), context capacity,"
" licence posture, optional measurement reference, and roles. Catalogue "
"validators require each runtime/role pair and default to resolve to an "
"eligible candidate, reject duplicate IDs, and order candidates weakest-"
"first within their runtime; larger models are explicit overrides. A "
"separate context floor is necessary for prompts that include an allow-"
"list and encoded page. Candidate and licence records "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/model_catalogue.py`) Role/runtime candidate model "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/model_catalogue.py`) Catalogue invariants "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/model_catalogue.py`) Bounded candidate ordering "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/model_catalogue.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:24
msgid ""
"The licence model requires publisher evidence (source URL and quote) for "
"verified entries and refuses an unverified commercial-use claim. The "
"shipped local defaults use Qwen3 entries declared Apache-2.0; research-"
"licensed Qwen2.5 candidates remain available only under non-commercial "
"posture or explicit override with an advisory. The hosted Claude Haiku "
"candidate is ordered by stated price and uses commercial service terms "
"rather than a fictitious weights licence. These are source-backed "
"declarations in code, not a current legal opinion. Most candidate "
"measurement references are empty, so the catalogue records capabilities, "
"prices, and vendor-published weight sizes but does not claim a broad "
"local benchmark corpus. Licence claim validator "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/model_catalogue.py`) Shipped candidates and stated "
"evidence (`src/cadrumo/core/model_catalogue.py`) Catalogue/default "
"consistency (`src/cadrumo/core/model_catalogue.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:26
msgid "Filing periods, notification facts, and workflow contracts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:28
msgid ""
"The period module separates registry coordinates from actual filing "
"periods. `RegistryPeriodCode` admits filing codes plus administrative "
"censo tokens and the symbolic `EVENT-N` selector; the narrower "
"`FilingPeriodCode` excludes those non-period coordinates. `Period` "
"combines a year and one filing code, derives cadence and inclusive date "
"spans only for quarterly/monthly/annual codes, and refuses span access "
"for instalment and extended event forms. Its year range is intentionally "
"wider than current registry coverage so callers can represent and then "
"refuse unsupported historical coordinates. Filing and registry "
"vocabularies (`src/cadrumo/core/period.py`) Registry-only tokens "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/period.py`) Period value and date semantics "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/period.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:30
msgid ""
"Notification service state is a pure projection from the delivery date, "
"read flag, explicit `as_of` date, and caller-supplied natural-day window."
" It distinguishes undelivered, accessed, still within the window, and "
"tacit rejection/deemed service. An undelivered row stays undelivered even"
" if a stray read flag is set; a missing read value is conservatively "
"treated as not accessed. Because the clock and threshold are explicit "
"inputs, re-evaluation is reproducible. Legal accuracy of the supplied "
"threshold is outside this module and was not independently checked. "
"Service-state vocabulary "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/notificacion_estado_servicio.py`) Pure service-state "
"resolver (`src/cadrumo/core/notificacion_estado_servicio.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:32
msgid ""
"`ObservedHeaderFact` preserves a token read from a submitted filing file "
"with its registry header key and byte-layout source locator. It "
"deliberately represents a header separately from a casilla, preserves the"
" unconverted value, omits blank fields, and refuses to attribute the fact"
" to a PDF or receipt. The source itself says disposition/marker shapes "
"have exporter evidence but refund and no-activity values lack bundled "
"AEAT facsimiles, so those values are not yet exercised against real "
"evidence. Header fact model (`src/cadrumo/core/observed_header_fact.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:34
msgid ""
"Other declared vocabularies keep the distinctions needed by callers: "
"Modelo syntax is only three ASCII digits and registry membership belongs "
"elsewhere; Modelo 232 related-party codes preserve AEAT's fixed-width "
"values and an explicit blank state; export artifacts distinguish "
"presentable BOE/XML files from local CSV/PDF calculation reports; "
"progress and action enums provide shared state names. Positive-result "
"payment elections are distinct from refund elections, with current-"
"account treatment explicitly described as refused until grounded. These "
"definitions constrain interfaces but do not prove that every consumer "
"enforces the corresponding policy. Modelo syntax boundary "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/modelo.py`) Modelo 232 coded fields "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/modelo_232_codigos.py`) Export artifact categories "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/modelo_export_artefact.py`) Payment choice "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/payment_election.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:36
msgid ""
"`post_filing_event.py` maps accent/case-folded AEAT subject text and a "
"coarse row type into a procedural category, with specific enforcement "
"terms taking priority over generic matches. A derived set marks "
"requerimientos, checks, sanctions, debts, and enforcement events "
"actionable. This is a read-only classification helper; substring matching"
" may need new patterns as portal wording changes and does not verify an "
"event's legal effect. `operations.py` declares lifecycle, terminal "
"result, committed-effect, durability, cancellation, deadline, close-"
"policy, event and interaction axes for supervised actions; it is a "
"contract vocabulary rather than an executor. Post-filing classification "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/post_filing_event.py`) Actionable categories and "
"classifier (`src/cadrumo/core/post_filing_event.py`) Operation lifecycle "
"and effect (`src/cadrumo/core/operations.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:38
msgid "Filesystem, extras, and precondition safeguards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:40
msgid ""
"Path helpers resolve relative operator paths against the platform user-"
"data anchor rather than the current working directory, normalize caller-"
"supplied storage roots, expose Windows long-path diagnostics, calculate "
"file-stat cache fingerprints and sum regular-file bytes. They explicitly "
"are not containment guards. A memoized `Path.resolve()` avoids repeated "
"syscalls, but the module notes that replacing a resolved real directory "
"with a symlink/junction changes resolution; if that happens after a "
"cached lookup, callers need to account for the stale resolution. The "
"retention selector is pure: age, count and byte bounds can be applied "
"sequentially or age/count as a union; callers own deletion. Protected "
"newest entries survive even when that leaves the total above a byte "
"ceiling. Project path resolution (`src/cadrumo/core/paths.py`) Storage-"
"root normalization (`src/cadrumo/core/paths.py`) Filesystem totals "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/paths.py`) Retention selection "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/paths.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:42
msgid ""
"Optional extras are probed by import spec without importing the package. "
"A single registry maps optional integrations to exclusive probe modules "
"and actionable install refusals; missing inner dependencies of an "
"installed package are not misclassified as an absent optional extra. "
"Package availability remains separate from user consent to use the "
"capability. Extra registry and probe "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/optional_extras.py`) Availability and classification "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/optional_extras.py`) Feature-boundary refusal "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/optional_extras.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:44
msgid ""
"`PreconditionEvidence` accepts stable fact-keyed scalar evidence, freezes"
" it in deterministic order, rejects presentation/action-like keys and raw"
" `aeat` command prose. Outcome invariants enforce unique evidence/action "
"argument identities, require evidence for the failed condition, require "
"exactly one of a recovery action or explicit no-recovery reason, and "
"verify that condition-evidence arguments exactly match the cited fact and"
" type. Missing argument names and conditionality must agree with the "
"actual bindings. This creates a meaningful boundary between factual "
"condition data and operator-facing recovery text. Factual evidence "
"constraints (`src/cadrumo/core/precondition_action_invariants.py`) "
"Outcome consistency checks "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/precondition_action_invariants.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:46
msgid ""
"The PID probe supports crash-recoverable locks by treating "
"permission/query failures as “alive” and reclaiming only when the OS "
"clearly reports a missing process. This is fail-safe against deleting "
"another holder's lock, though an uninspectable dead holder can delay "
"recovery. PID liveness probe (`src/cadrumo/core/pid_liveness.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:48
msgid "Assessment and follow-up"
msgstr "Evaluación y seguimiento"

#: ../../technical/articles/115-logging-output-privacy-model-selection-and-periods.md:50
msgid ""
"Strong local design choices include separate redaction paths for logs and"
" CLI output, explicit licence evidence and runtime-aware candidate "
"ranking, narrow filing-period grammars, reproducible notification-state "
"evaluation, and factual joins between action arguments and their cited "
"evidence. Main follow-up points are verifying the attached JSONL sink's "
"third-party DEBUG filtering, checking current vendor model facts and "
"licence pages against the catalogue, exercising unverified header values "
"against real AEAT artifacts, reviewing period/event classification "
"consumers against live portal vocabulary, and ensuring callers do not "
"treat path resolution as containment. No tests or runtime integrations "
"were executed in this pass; the chunk's declarations cannot certify end-"
"to-end coverage."
msgstr ""

